{
  "kanji": "右",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 右\ntitle: right\njlpt: 5\ntags: [jlpt-n5, grade-1, compound, starter]\nstrokes: 5\nradical: 口\nradicalNumber: 30\nonyomi: [ウ, ユウ]\nkunyomi: [みぎ]\ndistractors: [左, 口, 古]\n---\n\n# 右 — right\n\n**Strokes:** 5 · **Key (radical):** 口 (no. 30) · **JLPT:** N5 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n右 means \"right\" (the side, direction or hand) and, by extension, \"the above-mentioned\" in vertical writing, where 右 refers to what was written to the right.\nIt is usually analysed as a hand (the top part, a form of 又) over 口. The early forms are a hand, and the 口 was probably added\nlater; what it originally stood for (the mouth, a container) is debated. As a mnemonic: the right hand brings food to the mouth.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ウ | on | 右折 うせつ (right turn), 右翼 うよく (right wing) |\n| ユウ | on | [左右](../words/左右.md) さゆう (left and right), 右岸 うがん／ゆうがん |\n| みぎ | kun | [右手](../words/右手.md) みぎて, 右側 みぎがわ, 右に曲がる みぎにまがる |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [右手](../words/右手.md) みぎて — right hand\n- [左右](../words/左右.md) さゆう — left and right\n- 右側 みぎがわ — the right side\n\n## Notes\n\nIts opposite is [左](左.md). The pair is easy to mix up: 右 is written with the diagonal stroke (ノ) first and then the horizontal, and has 口 at the bottom;\nin 左 the horizontal comes first and 工 is at the bottom.\nDo not confuse 右 with 石 (stone, いし), where the diagonal starts at the left end of the top horizontal (厂 over 口) and the stroke order starts with the horizontal,\nnor with [古](古.md) (old), which has 十 over 口.\n",
